                <h1>Not a secret anymore: Atlantis goes all in on marketing</h1>
                
                <div class="article-deck">
                    After an unprecedented reveal on the world stage, Atlantis launches a massive marketing campaign.
                </div>

                <div class="byline">
                    <div class="byline-info">
                        By <a href="#" class="byline-name">Elena Rostova</a><br>
                        Published September 7, 2026 • Updated 12 minutes ago
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="hero-media">
                    <!-- A standard gray placeholder representing the UN broadcast -->
                    <img src="bill.png" alt="Live UN Broadcast">
                </div>
                <div class="hero-caption">
                    <span>CREDIT: UN WEB TV</span> | Digital billboards at Time Square, Manhattan display the Atlantis logo. 
                </div>

                <p><span class="article-location">UNITED NATIONS, New York</span> — The months of cryptic sonar leaks, unexplained coastal anomalies, and the rising tide of the grassroots 'Surfacers' protest movement culminated today in an event that has permanently altered the geopolitical landscape. The sovereign state of Atlantis has formally revealed itself to the surface world.</p>

                <p>However, the anticipated first contact scenario quickly dissolved into something much starker. The Atlantean delegation did not arrive in New York seeking a peace treaty, trade negotiations, or cultural exchange. They arrived to file a formal, comprehensively documented grievance.</p>

                <p>In a globally synchronized broadcast that overtook major commercial displays in Times Square, Piccadilly Circus, and Shibuya Crossing, the delegates assumed their newly arranged seats at the UN. Their opening remarks bypassed traditional diplomatic pleasantries entirely.</p>

                <div class="pull-quote">
                    "We have not emerged to ask for a seat at your table. We have taken one because the roof of our world has become a mass grave."
                </div>

                <p>The primary focus of the address was not their technology or their hidden history, but a meticulously compiled presentation of marine extinction. Referred to in previously leaked documents as the "Evidence Wall," a massive data visualization was projected behind the delegation, ticking through millions of data points tracking pollution, habitat collapse, and species loss dating back two centuries.</p>

                <p>The tone struck by the delegates was one of composed, state-level patience that has finally run out. Analysts are already noting that the Atlantean representatives framed the loss of ocean biodiversity not merely as an environmental tragedy, but as a deliberate and prolonged attack on their shared borders.</p>

                <p>As the emergency session continues, the digital wall behind the delegates relentlessly fills with the scientific names of extinct species—a scrolling testament leaving the assembly hall in stunned silence.</p>
            </article>
